Use daggers! It's a skill you can use the whole game. It's
not difficult to put together a stack of several daggers.
Like daggers will stack together even if they haven't been
IDed. Have your pet test one, name it "ok" if it's not
cursed and new daggers like that will stack. Later price ID
but do not ID or buc ID. Change the name to "+2 ok" or what
ever enchantment is appropriate.

I'm not a fan of the "hold your XL down" club. Just explore
each level thoroughly, not search for every secret closet,
just try to find all the rooms, then go down. Kill what
needs to be killed and let the XL vs. DL thing work itself
out. 

Use your pet, let him kill the 1 XP monsters. Ring around
Fido is a game you will enjoy more than the monster chasing
you.

Once you get Magicbane you should go far and it's guaranteed
as the first gift.

I wear the best magic friendly armor I can find, pet testing
everything leather or cloth. I would never consider crystal
plate because of the weight. With other classes I wear
mithril until I get my first set of dragon scales and then
add magic to my strategy, but the wizard can't afford to do
that.

Use Elbereth early and often. Grab a mirror, it has an
excellent chance of scaring away a monster that might
overpower you and if a nymph gets to you she will steal that
instead of something important.

